        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Besides polynomials, exponential and trigonometric functions are perhaps the most efficient functions in terms of calculating their definite integrals. Indeed, recall that the fundamental theorem of calculus states the following:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Besides polynomials, exponential and trigonometric functions are perhaps the most efficient functions in terms of calculating their definite integrals. Indeed, recall that the fundamental theorem of calculus states the following:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<blockquote><p><em>If <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)]</span> is a function that&#x27;s continuous on an interval <span class=\"math\">[MATH: [a,b]]</span>, and there exists a function <span class=\"math\">[MATH: F(x)]</span> such that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: F&#x27;(x) = f(x)]</span> on <span class=\"math\">[MATH: [a,b]]</span>, then</em>\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int_a^b f(x)\\,\\textrm{d}x = F(b) - F(a).]</span></p></blockquote>",
            "readable_text": "> If [MATH: f(x)] is a function that's continuous on an interval [MATH: [a,b]], and there exists a function [MATH: F(x)] such that [MATH: F'(x) = f(x)] on [MATH: [a,b]], then\n> [MATH: \\int_a^b f(x)\\,\\textrm{d}x = F(b) - F(a).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To illustrate this, let&#x27;s calculate\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\int_1^3  2^x \\,\\textrm{d}x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To illustrate this, let's calculate\n[MATH: \\int_1^3 2^x \\,\\textrm{d}x.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Recall that the antiderivative of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2^x]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln{2}}.]</span> Therefore, evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get </p>",
            "readable_text": "Recall that the antiderivative of [MATH: 2^x] is [MATH: \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln{2}}.] Therefore, evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{3}2^{x}dx|= (2^{x})/(\\ln 2)|_{1}^{3}; = (1)/(\\ln 2)(2^{3} \u2212 2^{1}); = (1)/(\\ln 2)(8 \u2212 2); = (6)/(\\ln 2).]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{3}2^{x}dx|= (2^{x})/(\\ln 2)|_{1}^{3}; = (1)/(\\ln 2)(2^{3} \u2212 2^{1}); = (1)/(\\ln 2)(8 \u2212 2); = (6)/(\\ln 2).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nBesides polynomials, exponential and trigonometric functions are perhaps the most efficient functions in terms of calculating their definite integrals. Indeed, recall that the fundamental theorem of calculus states the following:\n\nContent:\n> If [MATH: f(x)] is a function that's continuous on an interval [MATH: [a,b]], and there exists a function [MATH: F(x)] such that [MATH: F'(x) = f(x)] on [MATH: [a,b]], then\n> [MATH: \\int_a^b f(x)\\,\\textrm{d}x = F(b) - F(a).]\n\nContent:\nTo illustrate this, let's calculate\n[MATH: \\int_1^3 2^x \\,\\textrm{d}x.]\n\nContent:\nRecall that the antiderivative of [MATH: 2^x] is [MATH: \\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln{2}}.] Therefore, evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{3}2^{x}dx|= (2^{x})/(\\ln 2)|_{1}^{3}; = (1)/(\\ln 2)(2^{3} \u2212 2^{1}); = (1)/(\\ln 2)(8 \u2212 2); = (6)/(\\ln 2).]"
      },
      {
